==================================================
1. DOCUMENT STORAGE — IMPORTANT
==================================================

Change the document upload system so uploaded scholarship documents are stored DIRECTLY IN THE DATABASE instead of being permanently saved on the server disk.

Documents may include:
- Registration Form
- School ID
- Barangay Indigency
- Certificate of Grade (COG)
- Other scholarship requirements

Requirements:

- Store the actual binary file data in MySQL/MariaDB using LONGBLOB or an appropriate binary type.
- Store the original filename.
- Store MIME type.
- Store file size.
- Store upload date/time.
- Store the related application ID.
- Store document type.
- Store document verification status.
- Store rejection remarks when applicable.

The server must NOT permanently save uploaded documents in:
- uploads/
- documents/
- storage/
- public folders
- or any other permanent disk directory.

PHP's temporary upload file may exist during processing, but after the database insertion succeeds, the temporary file should not remain as permanent storage.

Use prepared statements and secure database handling.

If the existing database already has a documents table, MODIFY it instead of unnecessarily creating a duplicate table.

